# RGJ-RC1-010M — JavaSound-free ToneControl / Manager.playTone stage
#
# Scope
# -----
# Complete MIDP tone playback on RG35XX without javax.sound.midi. This stage uses
# the existing PlatformPlayer/ToneControl facade and the new pure-java
# RG35XXToneSequenceEncoder, then delegates the generated Standard MIDI File to
# RG35XXNativePlayer -> native TML/TSF.
#
# Source basis
# ------------
# - MIDP 2.0 ToneControl sequence grammar / parameter ranges (JSR-118)
# - upstream ToneControl constants in javax.microedition.media.control.ToneControl
# - exact upstream PlatformPlayer toneControl nested control and locator constructor
# - exact upstream Manager.playTone() JavaSound implementation
#
# PART A — encoder owner
# ----------------------
# `RG35XXToneSequenceEncoder` is the single RG35XX A-BNF tone-sequence -> SMF
# conversion owner. Do not create another tone synth or use javax.sound.midi.
#
# Supported MIDP grammar:
# - VERSION 1 (mandatory first attribute)
# - optional TEMPO modifier, valid 5..127, default 30 => 120 BPM
# - optional RESOLUTION, valid 1..127, default 64
# - BLOCK_START/BLOCK_END definitions 0..127
# - PLAY_BLOCK referencing only a previously defined block
# - SET_VOLUME 0..100
# - REPEAT multiplier 2..127 followed by exactly one tone event
# - note 0..127 or SILENCE, duration 1..127
#
# Block definitions are validated first and are not played by definition; only
# main sequence events and PLAY_BLOCK expansion produce MIDI events. Because a
# block may reference only an earlier block, expansion is acyclic. A fixed event
# expansion limit protects malformed/adversarial sequences.
#
# Timing identity:
#   MIDI PPQ = ToneControl resolution
#   MIDI ticks per tone duration unit = 4
#   tempo = tempoModifier * 4 BPM
# Therefore MIDI duration is exactly:
#   duration * 60 * 4 / (resolution * tempo) seconds
# which is the MIDP ToneControl formula.
#
# Output is SMF format 0, one track, channel 0, NOTE_ON/NOTE_OFF, CC7 volume and
# tempo meta. No JavaSound object is constructed.
#
# PART B — PlatformPlayer device://tone constructor
# ------------------------------------------------
# Existing upstream PlatformPlayer(String locator) creates a desktop midiPlayer
# for both device://tone and device://midi. On RG35XX, intercept TONE locator
# before that construction:
#
#   contentType = "audio/x-tone-seq";
#   rg35xxPlayer = new RG35XXNativePlayer(
#       new ByteArrayInputStream(new byte[0]), contentType);
#   controls[0] = existing facade volumeControl adapted to native backend;
#   controls[3] = existing toneControl adapted to native backend;
#
# `device://midi` live-message control is NOT claimed by this stage because the
# current native protocol registers complete MIDI blobs and has no live MIDI
# short-message opcode. It must not fall through to JavaSound on RG35XX.
#
# PART C — existing ToneControl facade
# ------------------------------------
# Keep PlatformPlayer's existing nested `toneControl` as the public Control owner.
# Add an RG35XX branch; do not create a parallel javax ToneControl class.
#
# setSequence(byte[] sequence) on RG35XX:
# 1. if sequence == null -> IllegalArgumentException
# 2. if facade state is PREFETCHED or STARTED -> IllegalStateException, per MIDP
# 3. if sequence begins MThd, copy/use it as an already-converted SMF
# 4. otherwise call RG35XXToneSequenceEncoder.encode(sequence)
# 5. call rg35xxPlayer.setMidi(midiBytes)
#
# Invalid A-BNF input propagates IllegalArgumentException from the encoder.
# No javax.sound.midi Sequence/Track/ShortMessage objects are used on RG35XX.
#
# PART D — Manager.playTone()
# ---------------------------
# At the top of existing Manager.playTone(note,duration,volume):
# - preserve argument validation (note 0..127, duration >0, volume clamp 0..100)
# - preserve upstream compatibility policy that durations below 50 ms use an
#   effective duration of 50 ms (several games rely on very short audible cues)
# - if RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive(), bypass toneChannel/toneThread entirely
# - generate SMF from that same effective duration with
#     RG35XXToneSequenceEncoder.encodeSingleTone(note,effectiveDuration,volume)
# - keep one Manager-owned transient RG35XXNativePlayer for playTone; close the
#   previous transient before replacing it so repeated calls do not leak players
# - bind one reusable event listener; on native END_OF_MEDIA close/release the
#   transient player if its id is still the active one
# - realize/prefetch/start and return immediately (non-blocking)
#
# This preserves the single-current-tone behavior and duration compatibility of
# upstream's interrupted toneThread without creating a Java sleep thread on RG35XX.
#
# PART E — capability promotion
# -----------------------------
# After this stage, RG35XXMediaProfile may advertise `audio/x-tone-seq` because:
# - the public ToneControl grammar has a JavaSound-free converter;
# - `device://tone` is routed before desktop midiPlayer creation;
# - converted bytes are registered through the already-proven native MIDI path;
# - Manager.playTone has a nonblocking native route.
#
# This promotion does not imply device://midi live MIDI control support.
#
# PART F — lifecycle and event ownership
# --------------------------------------
# Tone players use the same RG35XXMediaRegistry/event return channel as MIDI/WAV.
# LOOPED remains STARTED; END_OF_MEDIA moves PREFETCHED and releases transient
# Manager.playTone players. Game unload RESET clears the registry/native media.
#
# PlatformPlayer.notifyListeners remains the sole MIDP/vendor fanout. Tone encoder
# never invokes listeners.
#
# PART G — compatibility / performance invariants
# -----------------------------------------------
# - no javax.sound.midi on RG35XX tone path
# - no toneThread / sleep timer on RG35XX
# - no extra synth or native ring
# - encoder allocations occur only during setSequence/playTone setup
# - no heap allocation in native render callback
# - desktop Manager/PlatformPlayer tone path remains unchanged when target false
# - device://midi is not falsely promoted by this stage
#
# BUILD-PASS remains pending exact source application and Ant/native build.
